description:
Write lesson 1.04's parameter macros as functions, on 64-bit Windows types:

```cpp
using WPARAM = std::uint64_t;
using LPARAM = std::int64_t;
using UINT = std::uint32_t;

LPARAM makeLParam(int lo, int hi);       // the low 16 bits of each, packed into the low 32 bits
int loWord(LPARAM v);                    // unsigned: 0 .. 65535
int hiWord(LPARAM v);
int getX(LPARAM v);                      // signed: -32768 .. 32767, like GET_X_LPARAM
int getY(LPARAM v);
std::string messageRange(UINT msg);
```

`messageRange` names the range a message number belongs to: `"system"` below `0x0400` (`WM_USER`), `"class"` from `0x0400` to `0x7FFF`, `"app"` from `0x8000` (`WM_APP`) to `0xBFFF`, `"registered"` from `0xC000` to `0xFFFF`, and `"reserved"` above.

